4. United States Government data
--------------------------------

Sources items 1, 2, 5, 6, 8 and 15 are United States Government or NASA
material. Most is public domain and cannot be placed under any licence, but
citation is requested: NASA for GISTEMP and GloSSAC, NOAA GML for the Mauna Loa
CO2 record. Item 15, the RONI series, carried an open question about citation; resolved in
v1.7.10, CPC requests none. The series ships with this package as
RONI.v5.ascii.txt, checksummed in the manifest.

Items 3 and 4, the two total solar irradiance series, are governed by the NOAA
Climate Data Record use agreement. Resolved in v1.7.11 against the agency's own
document, UseAgreement_01B-32.pdf, "Fair Use of NOAA's CDR Data Sets, Algorithms
and Documentation", which states that "the CDR data sets are non-proprietary,
publicly available, and no restrictions are placed upon their use". Citation and
acknowledgement are urged rather than required and there is no notification
requirement, so redistributing these values is permitted. The one carve-out is
the CDR production software, which that document places outside the Open Data
policies and which this package does not ship.

Items 13 and 14, CERES EBAF and the NCEI ocean heat content series, had no terms,
location or citation recorded at all until v1.7.11. All three are now recorded:
NASA data openly available with citation requested for CERES, cite Loeb et al.
(2018); US Government work in the public domain with citation requested for the
NCEI series, cite Levitus et al. (2012).
